From 5b841857dae74a237d0637e2c86f607214a58210 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:36:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi-0172-sweet-files-server

A file server for the running iOS root over USB Ethernet (tcp 2223 on ue0,
192.168.7.2), so test binaries and tools can be installed without
reflashing the root image: PUT/GET/MKDIR/LINK/RM/CHMOD, one request per
connection. Ported from ios-flame patch 0091 (bsd/dev/sweet_files.c, xnu-8796
as here); started from sweet_usb_gadget_start (boot-arg sweetfiles=0 off)
when the interface is up, with sweet_vfs_mkdir/symlink/unlink wrappers in
vfs_syscalls.c. umi has no USB command channel to ask for a sync, so every
request that changes the file system is followed by sync(), so what it
wrote survives the reset that ends a fastboot-boot test cycle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
